From eb7923981d128431e4c711f2d107ae5451fd34fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 17:24:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v3.0.8: the backup file guarded five ways; park the idle
 AiMesh backhaul

Backup & Restore (httpd/web.c, Reaper_Backup.asp, RBKP_37-49 x25):
- Sealed backups: either export can be wrapped in an AES-256-GCM container
  keyed from a passphrase (scrypt 32768/8/1); the two header lines are the
  authenticated additional data, so a wrong passphrase and an altered byte
  are refused identically before anything is parsed. A sealed .rbk keeps its
  inner header (rbk_up.base offsets every part read); a sealed settings file
  is opened on the router (same model: settings + reboot; other model: the
  no-reboot Reaper import) instead of the browser rebuild. Plain files and
  older archives restore unchanged. The passphrase is never stored.
- Re-authentication on export: the admin password rides in the POST body and
  is checked in the download handler itself (compare_passwd_in_shadow); the
  page pre-checks it (action=reauth) so a wrong answer is a message, not a
  one-line file. Five failures lock exports for a minute.
- Client address on every export, import and refusal log line.
- Each card names the credentials its file carries.
- /jffs restore refuses a member written through an earlier symlink member
  (ec jffslink) - the one traversal busybox tar does not strip.

AiMesh backhaul parking (rc/amaspark.c, Reaper_Wireless.asp, RWIF_85-93 x25):
- Measured on the RT-BE96U with no node paired: every band's primary is up,
  hidden, carrying the MAINBH SSID; on 2.4/5 GHz each BSS beacons on its own
  (txbcnfrm = 3 streams vs 1 on 6 GHz), so the idle carrier is a full beacon
  stream and a WPA listener with a blob-derived key. `wl bss down` on the
  primary leaves the virtual BSSs serving every client.
- Opt-in daemon (amas_bh_park): parks the 2.4/5 GHz primaries while this is
  the AiMesh primary, no node is paired and no search is running; releases
  within 5 s when cfg_obstatus leaves idle (search/add node), on a paired
  node, on disable, on stop; re-parks when the window closes without a node;
  20-min stuck-window cap; never 6 GHz; only releases what it parked. Every
  transition is a syslog line with interface, band and reason.
- rc applet + /sbin symlink, restart_amaspark service, Wireless page panel.

